    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0816" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/1253</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Mexican Affairs,
                        Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Mr. Summerlin writes as
                    follows in a private letter to me dated October 19: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Mr. de la Huerta seems to be the prime mover in having an organic law on
                            petroleum drawn up. … The draft has already been subject to many changes
                            and will continue to be. I have promised Pani a copy of the latest draft
                            I have … and he has promised to let me know if it is official.</p>
                        <p>“Again, last night, Pani said that they would welcome ‘honest criticism’
                            (these are my words put into his mouth) of the proposed law. However, as
                            I see it, why should we devote time and ammunition on drafts that are
                            being changed daily? I have made a personal request of Pani for an
                            official copy of the proposed law.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">atthew</hi>] E. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">anna</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
